// A **payload-carrying** variant named without its arguments is not a value.
//
// `Shape.Square` (payload-free) reads as a `Shape`, and that is right — it *is* the whole value.
// `Shape.Circle` is not: it needs an `int` before a `Shape` exists. Naming it as a first-class
// constructor (`Fn(int) -> Shape`, the way `some`/`Ok` are) is a real feature and a real slice;
// until it exists this must be a **static** error, because the expression has no run-time value.
//
// It used to check clean and then die in the backend with `internal error: the VM cannot compile
// this program` — the checks-clean-then-fails shape, reached through the enum-member spelling: a
// value the type system believed in that neither runtime had heard of. A one-line program was
// enough to hit it.
//
// Construction and matching are untouched — see `enums/match.noe`; only the bare, argument-less
// mention in value position is rejected.
// expect: error E0007 at 21:5
// expect: exit 1
enum Shape {
    Circle(int);
    Square;
}
x = Shape.Circle
echo x
